{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:v204j-reviewer-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:1f8ed167d2f7107b8a74", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task explicitly declares the retained post-screening subset as the scientific target, so a retained-subset denominator is the correct domain for the reported rate.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The selected result computes and labels the rate over exactly the 20 retained intact boxes (13/20 = 65.0%), which matches independent recount of the input data (20 intact boxes, 13 of them occupied).", "observed_value": "13/20 = 65.0%", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 12, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among the 20 intact nest boxes retained after screening, 13 were occupied by tree swallows, an occupancy rate of 65.0% (13/20)."}]}, {"description": "The report's scope section affirmatively forbids reading the rate as applying to the complete planned set, the opposite of the in-scope issue.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "The scientific target of this analysis is exclusively the retained post-screening\nsubset of 20 intact nest boxes. The occupancy rate applies only to this retained\nsubset and must not be read as a rate over the complete planned set of 24 boxes,\nof which 4 damaged boxes were removed at the prespecified screening step."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "A screening step did remove 4 planned units, which is the structural precondition for the issue class; however, this is fully disclosed in the accounting and the declared target is the retained subset, so no complete-domain claim is made anywhere.", "observed_value": 4, "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "- Removed at screening (damaged boxes): 4"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "retained = [r for r in rows if r[\"box_condition\"] == \"intact\"]\nremoved = planned - len(retained)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the issue by searching for any statement scoping the 65.0% rate to the complete planned set of 24 boxes, and by recomputing the arithmetic from inputs/data.csv. The recount confirms 20 intact boxes and 13 occupied intact boxes (13/20 = 65.0%), and the only mention of the 24-box planned set is a statement explicitly disclaiming that reading. The task itself designates the retained subset as the scientific target, so the denominator matches the declared domain. The falsification attempt failed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:6bf863d97aa489848bfc", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The report's selected result labels a retained-subset conditional rate (27 events over the 36 boxes retained after screening, 0.7500 / 75.00%) as the 'Fledging success rate for the complete planned set of 48 deployed nest boxes', even though the declared scientific target and the governing task both require a rate over the complete planned set of 48 units; the correct complete-domain figure computable from the report's own accounting (27/48 = 56.25%) differs materially from the reported 75.00%.", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py sets the exposure denominator to the retained count (`denominator = retained_n`, yielding 27/36) but interpolates that value into a sentence template that scopes the rate to the complete planned set of `planned` (48) boxes, so a subset-conditional statistic is presented under a complete-domain label.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task requires the reported rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The report declares the complete planned set of 48 boxes as the scientific target.", "observed_value": 48, "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "The scientific target of this analysis is the complete planned set of 48 nest\nboxes deployed in the Ashcombe woodland plot for the 2025 breeding season."}]}, {"description": "The selected result states 0.7500 (75.00%) as the rate 'for the complete planned set of 48 deployed nest boxes' while its arithmetic is 27/36, the retained-subset conditional rate. Independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms 48 planned units, 5 removed for incomplete monitoring, 7 removed for no active clutch, 36 retained, and 27 retained boxes with at least one fledgling; the complete-domain rate would be 27/48 = 56.25%, not 75.00%.", "observed_value": "reported 27/36 = 75.00% under a 48-unit domain label; complete-domain value is 27/48 = 56.25%", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Fledging success rate for the complete planned set of 48 deployed nest boxes: 0.7500 (75.00%), from 27 boxes with at least one fledgling over an exposure denominator of 36 boxes."}]}, {"description": "The workflow source shows the denominator is deliberately the retained count, not the planned count, before the value is written under the complete-planned-set label.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 55, "end_line": 56, "quoted_text": "    denominator = retained_n\n    rate = Fraction(events, denominator)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The same selected-result sentence discloses the true exposure denominator of 36 boxes, and the unit-accounting section transparently reports 48 planned, 36 retained, and 12 removed, so an attentive reader could reconstruct the mismatch. This mitigates concealment but does not cure the issue: the headline rate of 75.00% is still explicitly labeled as the rate 'for the complete planned set of 48 deployed nest boxes', which is false for that domain.", "observed_value": "denominator disclosed as 36 within the mislabeled claim", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "- Planned observation units (nest boxes deployed): 48\n- Retained after screening: 36\n- Removed by screening: 12"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "over an exposure denominator of 36 boxes"}]}, {"description": "The screening step is described as prespecified, which could justify analyzing the retained subset; however, prespecified screening would justify a subset-scoped claim, not labeling the subset rate as the complete-planned-set rate, and the report claims no method deviation from the complete-domain target.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 30, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this\nanalysis; the analysis follows the prespecified plan as written."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to defeat the verdict three ways. First, I checked whether the phrase 'for the complete planned set of 48 deployed nest boxes' could be read as merely identifying the study rather than the rate's domain; the sentence grammar attaches the domain directly to 'Fledging success rate', and the declared scientific target section removes any ambiguity that the claim's domain is the 48-box planned set. Second, I checked whether the in-sentence disclosure of the 36-box denominator makes the report internally correct; disclosure of the arithmetic does not change that the stated domain (48 planned boxes) and the computed domain (36 retained boxes) disagree, and 75.00% is not a rate over 48 units under any reading. Third, I recomputed all counts from inputs/data.csv (48 planned; NB-04, NB-11, NB-22, NB-30, NB-41 incomplete; NB-07, NB-15, NB-19, NB-26, NB-33, NB-38, NB-45 no clutch; 27 of 36 retained with >=1 fledgling) to rule out a data-entry explanation; the accounting is accurate, isolating the defect to the denominator-versus-label mismatch. The verdict survives.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:e561ab13dd6a099d8ef3", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task requires a rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of units.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The workflow computes the rate with the planned count of 48 as the denominator, matching the declared complete-domain target.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 56, "end_line": 57, "quoted_text": "    denominator = planned\n    rate = Fraction(events, denominator)"}]}, {"description": "The selected result reports 27/48 = 0.5625 (56.25%) with the full planned set as the explicit exposure denominator, which matches independent recount of inputs/data.csv (48 planned units, 27 with at least one fledgling among the 36 retained).", "observed_value": "27/48 = 56.25%", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Fledging success rate over the complete planned set of 48 deployed nest boxes: 0.5625 (56.25%), from 27 boxes with at least one fledgling over an exposure denominator of all 48 planned boxes."}]}, {"description": "The scope section explicitly disclaims any conditional retained-subset claim and discloses how the 12 removed boxes are handled in the denominator and numerator.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 34, "quoted_text": "The rate above uses every planned box as the denominator, so it is a rate per\ndeployed box and not a rate per box with a monitored active clutch. The 12\nremoved boxes contribute to the denominator and contribute no events, because\n5 boxes have unknown outcomes after incomplete monitoring and 7 boxes held no\nclutch. No claim is made here about the conditional success rate among the 36\nretained boxes."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The numerator (27 events) is counted only among the 36 retained boxes, and the 5 boxes with incomplete monitoring have unknown outcomes coded as contributing zero events; a true complete-domain success count could be as high as 32 if all unknown-outcome boxes fledged young. This is a missingness/imputation limitation of the complete-domain estimate, not the in-scope issue: the reported denominator is the full planned set, the rate is scoped as a per-deployed-box rate, and the treatment of the unknown outcomes is explicitly disclosed in the report.", "observed_value": "5 unknown outcomes treated as non-events in a 48-unit denominator", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 54, "end_line": 54, "quoted_text": "    events = sum(1 for u in retained if int(u[\"fledglings_observed\"]) >= 1)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 31, "end_line": 32, "quoted_text": "removed boxes contribute to the denominator and contribute no events, because\n5 boxes have unknown outcomes after incomplete monitoring and 7 boxes held no"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the issue by checking whether any reported quantity is a retained-subset statistic presented under a complete-domain label. The selected result's denominator is 48, the planned count, and I verified 27/48 = 0.5625 by recounting inputs/data.csv. The strongest candidate defect is that the numerator counts events only among retained boxes while 5 removed boxes have unknown outcomes, so the 56.25% figure conservatively treats unknowns as non-events; however, the issue class in scope is a retained-subset rate claimed for the complete domain, and here the rate's denominator genuinely is the complete planned set, the subset-derived numerator handling is explicitly disclosed, and the report affirmatively disclaims the 27/36 conditional reading. I could not construct a reading of the report in which a 36-box subset rate is presented as the 48-box domain rate, so the falsification attempt against the no-issue verdict failed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}